  "docs.rateLimits.title": "Rate Limits",
  "docs.rateLimits.intro": "To protect upstream stability and prevent any single user from monopolizing resources, {name} applies rate limits across several dimensions. This page helps you understand what triggers them, read the response headers, and design a sensible backoff strategy.",
  "docs.rateLimits.dimensionsHeading": "Rate Limit Dimensions",
  "docs.rateLimits.dimRpm": " (Requests Per Minute): the total number of requests you can make per minute.",
  "docs.rateLimits.dimTpm": " (Tokens Per Minute): the total number of tokens you can consume per minute (input + output combined).",
  "docs.rateLimits.dimConcurrencyLabel": "Concurrency",
  "docs.rateLimits.dimConcurrency": ": the maximum number of in-flight requests at any given moment.",
  "docs.rateLimits.dimUpstreamLabel": "Upstream-side limits",
  "docs.rateLimits.dimUpstream": ": rate limits the upstream provider applies to the {name} account, passed through to you. The exact thresholds vary by model.",
  "docs.rateLimits.calloutBothTitle": "Enforced at Both the Key and Account Level",
  "docs.rateLimits.calloutBothPart1": "Limits are settled across two layers, \"per-Key\" and \"per-account\" — hitting the cap on either layer triggers a",
  "docs.rateLimits.calloutBothPart2": ". You can set a separate cap for each Key on the \"",
  "docs.rateLimits.calloutBothPart3": "\" page to isolate high-risk workloads.",
  "docs.rateLimits.triggerHeading": "What a Trigger Looks Like",
  "docs.rateLimits.triggerIntroPart1": "When rate limited, the response returns",
  "docs.rateLimits.triggerIntroPart2": " plus a standard error body:",
  "docs.rateLimits.headersIntro": "The response headers also include some helpful hint fields:",
  "docs.rateLimits.thHeader": "Response Header",
  "docs.rateLimits.thMeaning": "Meaning",
  "docs.rateLimits.hdrLimitRequests": "Maximum requests allowed in the current window",
  "docs.rateLimits.hdrRemainingRequests": "Requests remaining in this window",
  "docs.rateLimits.hdrResetRequests": "How long until this window resets (seconds)",
  "docs.rateLimits.hdrLimitTokens": "Maximum tokens allowed to be consumed in the current window",
  "docs.rateLimits.hdrRemainingTokens": "Tokens remaining",
  "docs.rateLimits.hdrRetryAfter": "Suggested number of seconds to wait before retrying, per RFC 7231",
  "docs.rateLimits.backoffHeading": "Recommended Backoff Strategy",
  "docs.rateLimits.backoffIntroPart1": "When you hit a",
  "docs.rateLimits.backoffIntroPart2": ", handle it in the following order of preference:",
  "docs.rateLimits.backoffStep1Part1": "Check the",
  "docs.rateLimits.backoffStep1Part2": "response header or the",
  "docs.rateLimits.backoffStep1Part3": "in the error message, and wait the full duration before sending again.",
  "docs.rateLimits.backoffStep2Part1": "When no wait time is specified, use ",
  "docs.rateLimits.backoffStep2Strong": "exponential backoff with jitter",
  "docs.rateLimits.backoffStep2Part2": ": ",
  "docs.rateLimits.backoffStep2Part3": ", with up to 5 retries.",
  "docs.rateLimits.backoffStep3": "If retries still fail → fall back to another model of the same type, or queue the work for background processing.",
  "docs.rateLimits.quotaHeading": "Raising Your Quota",
  "docs.rateLimits.quotaKeyPart1": "A single Key's",
  "docs.rateLimits.quotaKeyPart2": "can be adjusted directly on the",
  "docs.rateLimits.quotaKeyPart3": "page — just increase it.",
  "docs.rateLimits.quotaAccount": "Account-level RPM / TPM is determined by your group policy. For a larger quota, contact your administrator to adjust your user group.",
  "docs.rateLimits.quotaConcurrency": "For high-concurrency workloads, we recommend spreading the load across \"multiple Keys + client-side rotation\" to avoid maxing out a single Key.",
  "docs.rateLimits.calloutWarnTitle": "Don't Blindly Retry at High Concurrency",
  "docs.rateLimits.calloutWarnBody": "Retrying immediately with no delay after a 429 will just earn you more 429s and slow recovery down. The backoff strategy above is a minimum baseline; for production we recommend using a task queue (BullMQ / Celery) to smooth out spikes.",
  "docs.rateLimits.codeCommentPreferRetryAfter": "Prefer retry_after from the response",
