  "docs.streaming.title": "Streaming Responses",
  "docs.streaming.introPrefix": "Add",
  "docs.streaming.introSuffix": "to your request and {name} will push tokens incrementally over the standard Server-Sent Events (SSE) protocol. Any OpenAI-compatible client recognizes this format with no extra adaptation needed.",
  "docs.streaming.enableTitle": "How to Enable",
  "docs.streaming.curlNDesc": "tells curl not to buffer, so you can watch tokens stream out one by one in your terminal.",
  "docs.streaming.sseFormatTitle": "SSE Message Format",
  "docs.streaming.sseFormatDescPrefix": "Each event starts with",
  "docs.streaming.sseFormatDescSuffix": "and a blank line marks the end of an event:",
  "docs.streaming.bulletDeltaPrefix": "After each",
  "docs.streaming.bulletDeltaMid": "comes a JSON payload whose field structure matches the",
  "docs.streaming.bulletDeltaMid2": "in non-streaming responses, except that",
  "docs.streaming.bulletDeltaMid3": "is replaced with",
  "docs.streaming.bulletDeltaSuffix": ".",
  "docs.streaming.bulletConcatPrefix": "Concatenate all the",
  "docs.streaming.bulletConcatSuffix": "values to get the final text.",
  "docs.streaming.bulletDonePrefix": "The last event is the string literal",
  "docs.streaming.bulletDoneSuffix": "; the client can close the connection once it reads this.",
  "docs.streaming.bulletUsage": "field usually appears in the second-to-last event.",
  "docs.streaming.calloutUsageTitle": "Why usage arrives last",
  "docs.streaming.calloutUsageBodyPrefix": "Under the streaming protocol, the output token count can only be measured accurately once the model stops generating, so",
  "docs.streaming.calloutUsageBodySuffix": "appears exactly once, in the final frame.",
  "docs.streaming.clientParseTitle": "Client-Side Parsing",
  "docs.streaming.clientParseDescPrefix": "Every OpenAI SDK already handles SSE parsing for you—just consume it directly with a",
  "docs.streaming.clientParseDescSuffix": "loop or iterator:",
  "docs.streaming.tabFetchLabel": "Native fetch (Browser)",
  "docs.streaming.pitfallsTitle": "Common Pitfalls",
  "docs.streaming.pitfallProxyTitle": "A reverse proxy buffered the stream",
  "docs.streaming.pitfallProxyBodyPrefix": "If you run {name} behind Nginx / a load balancer / Cloudflare, make sure they do not buffer",
  "docs.streaming.pitfallProxyBodyMid": "responses. With Nginx you need at least",
  "docs.streaming.pitfallProxyBodyAnd": "and",
  "docs.streaming.pitfallProxyBodySuffix": ", otherwise you'll see the \"long wait, then everything dumped at once\" behavior.",
  "docs.streaming.pitfallReadTitle": "The client must keep reading",
  "docs.streaming.pitfallReadBodyPrefix": "A streaming request is a long-lived connection; the client must keep reading until",
  "docs.streaming.pitfallReadBodySuffix": ". If you disconnect midway, {name} will keep sending to the upstream (until the upstream finishes) to avoid missed billing, so \"disconnect ≠ stop billing\"—keep this in mind.",
  "docs.streaming.footerPrefix": "If your SSE stream gets truncated midway or returns invalid JSON, go to the",
  "docs.streaming.footerConsoleLogs": "Console Logs",
  "docs.streaming.footerMid": "to view the upstream response for the corresponding request ID, or refer to",
  "docs.streaming.footerErrorCodes": "Error Codes",
  "docs.streaming.footerSuffix": ".",
